            "table": null,
            "text": "Microsoft 365 Commercial Products and Cloud Services",
            "text_hash": "36240328251d3e3edca2a5974ea6b3fc18b4246f88dd197ae89a9a390b9f78c9",
            "type": "heading_candidate"
          },
          {
            "block_id": "block-000101-67803298",
            "dom_path": "/html/body/div[15]/p[9]",
            "image_asset_id": null,
            "layout_role": null,
            "ordinal": 101,
            "reported_page": 5,
            "source_anchor": "F_52de2956-2cf6-4683-90c8-0b4adeb07187",
            "style_signature": [
              [
                "font-family",
                "times new roman"
              ],
              [
                "font-size",
                "10pt"
              ],
              [
                "margin-top",
                "9pt"
              ],
              [
                "text-align",
                "justify"
              ]
            ],
            "table": null,
            "text": "Microsoft 365 Commercial is an AI-powered business and productivity solutions platform that brings together Office, Windows, Microsoft 365 Copilot, and Enterprise Mobility + Security to help organizations empower their employees. Growth depends on our ability to reach new users in new markets such as frontline workers, small and medium businesses, and growth markets, as well as add AI-enabled tools, features, and agentic scenarios to our core product and service offerings across communication, collaboration, analytics, security, compliance, and other AI business productivity categories. Microsoft 365 Commercial revenue is mainly affected by a combination of continued installed base growth and average revenue per user expansion, as well as the continued shift from Office licensed on-premises to Microsoft 365.",
            "text_hash": "6780329863d5a23515b01856bcfff1f74f2385faa41f706c61c225db9bb34eb0",
            "type": "paragraph"
          },
          {
            "block_id": "block-000102-83762012",
            "dom_path": "/html/body/div[15]/p[10]",
            "image_asset_id": null,
            "layout_role": null,
            "ordinal": 102,
            "reported_page": 5,
            "source_anchor": "F_52de2956-2cf6-4683-90c8-0b4adeb07187",
            "style_signature": [
              [
                "font-family",
                "times new roman"
              ],
              [
                "font-size",
                "10pt"
              ],
              [
                "font-style",
                "italic"
              ],
              [
                "font-weight",
                "bold"
              ],
              [
                "margin-top",
                "13.5pt"
              ],
              [
                "text-align",
                "left"
              ]
            ],
            "table": null,
            "text": "Microsoft 365 Consumer Products and Cloud Services",
            "text_hash": "83762012f8b897dcd83bb7b213cedc91a00afae988230bf9a0ac4a8220e0fd1d",
            "type": "heading_candidate"
          },
          {
            "block_id": "block-000103-a597bcd9",
            "dom_path": "/html/body/div[15]/p[11]",
            "image_asset_id": null,
            "layout_role": null,
            "ordinal": 103,
            "reported_page": 5,
            "source_anchor": "F_52de2956-2cf6-4683-90c8-0b4adeb07187",
            "style_signature": [
              [
                "font-family",
                "times new roman"
              ],
              [
                "font-size",
                "10pt"
              ],
              [
                "margin-top",
                "9pt"
              ],
              [
                "text-align",
                "justify"
              ]
            ],
            "table": null,
            "text": "Microsoft 365 Consumer is designed to increase personal productivity and creativity through a range of products and services. Growth depends on our ability to reach new users, add value to our core product set with new features including AI tools, and continue to expand our product and service offerings into new markets. Microsoft 365 Consumer cloud revenue and Office Consumer products revenue is mainly affected by the percentage of customers that buy Office with their new devices and the continued shift from Office licensed on-premises to Microsoft 365 Consumer subscriptions. Microsoft 365 Consumer cloud revenue is also affected by the demand for communication and storage through Outlook.com and OneDrive, which is largely driven by subscriptions and advertising.",
            "text_hash": "a597bcd909f9d5f121109e41762ff47af22edb5f1504c614244496d41bd98765",
            "type": "paragraph"
          },
          {
